WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.776
Silicon Valley forgot

00:00:01.588 --> 00:00:02.566
its customers

00:00:03.102 --> 00:00:03.939
In a lecture

00:00:03.751 --> 00:00:04.953
at Johns Hopkins

00:00:04.765 --> 00:00:06.616
in October 2026

00:00:06.781 --> 00:00:08.208
Tim O'Reilly traces

00:00:08.019 --> 00:00:09.434
Silicon Valley's move

00:00:09.246 --> 00:00:10.554
from customer-centered

00:00:10.366 --> 00:00:12.017
innovation to extraction

00:00:11.828 --> 00:00:13.208
driven by shareholder

00:00:13.019 --> 00:00:13.998
capitalism

00:00:14.518 --> 00:00:15.402
He started his

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:16.180
company more than

00:00:15.992 --> 00:00:17.171
40 years ago with

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.881
a 500-dollar investment

00:00:18.987 --> 00:00:19.753
and launched the

00:00:19.565 --> 00:00:20.768
first web portal

00:00:20.579 --> 00:00:22.065
in 1993

00:00:22.598 --> 00:00:24.060
Now he argues

00:00:23.978 --> 00:00:25.263
monopoly ambitions

00:00:25.074 --> 00:00:26.064
and hype shape

00:00:25.876 --> 00:00:26.937
the AI boom

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:27.869
a far cry

00:00:27.681 --> 00:00:28.588
from the valley's

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:29.343
early days

00:00:29.862 --> 00:00:30.876
Full story on

00:00:30.687 --> 00:00:31.583
the dashboard
